<%# The rows the rejection changed (TransfersController#redrawn_entries): the
    match's legs, loaded after it was destroyed (the transfer's own legs still
    hold it in memory and would draw its pill again), and any row the
    "Transfer?" hint now pairs with them. Each row holds its category menus and
    match controls, so redrawing the row is enough. Rows are drawn in the
    page's view (an account page signs a transfer's amount, other lists show
    +/-). %>
<% @redrawn_entries.each do |entry| %>
  <%= turbo_stream.replace entry, partial: "entries/entry", locals: { entry: entry, view_ctx: @view_ctx } %>
<% end %>
